### FINDING 1 — FATAL — location: "Statement refuted" section, final sentence
CLAIM AS WRITTEN: "The comparison worth keeping in view is the closed family
$[0, 1/k]$, which differs only by the inclusion of the left endpoint and
intersects in $\{0\}$; that computation is the preceding example on this
page."

WHY IT FAILS: This asserts a reading-order fact — that
`ex-nested-intervals-single-point` (the $[0,1/k]$ computation) is the item
immediately preceding `cex-nested-open-intervals-empty` on their shared page.
It is not. The page's frontmatter (`library/real-analysis/monotone-sequences-and-cauchy-completeness-examples.md`), whose `examples:` array SCHEMA.md
documents as "Section 5, in reading order," lists:

```
examples: [ex-babylonian-sqrt-two, ex-recursive-sqrt-two-plus-x,
           ex-nested-intervals-single-point, ex-two-subsequential-limits,
           ex-contractive-sequence-fixed-point,
           cex-cauchy-rationals-no-rational-limit,
           cex-nested-open-intervals-empty, cex-nested-unbounded-closed-empty, ...]
```

`ex-nested-intervals-single-point` is position 3; `cex-nested-open-intervals-empty`
is position 7. The item immediately preceding it is
`cex-cauchy-rationals-no-rational-limit`, not `ex-nested-intervals-single-point`.
Even under the looser reading "the preceding item of kind *example*," the
nearest one is `ex-contractive-sequence-fixed-point` (position 5), still not
`ex-nested-intervals-single-point`. Three items sit between the claimed
"preceding" item and this one under any reading. The mathematical content of
the comparison itself is accurate (I checked `ex-nested-intervals-single-point`
on disk: it does compute $\bigcap_{k\ge1}[0,1/k] = \{0\}$), but the assertion
about *where it sits relative to this item* is false and would mislead a
reader trying to locate it.

WHAT WOULD FIX IT: Either drop "on this page" positional language and simply
say "the closed family ... is computed in [[ex-nested-intervals-single-point]]"
(a plain citation, no ordering claim), or correct the wording to name the
actual immediately preceding item / the true relative position.

